---
import AppLayout from '../../../../ui/layouts/AppLayout.astro'; import { laboratoryReadDependencies } from '../../../../modules/laboratory/application/dependencies.js';const actor=Astro.locals.actor;if(!actor)return Astro.redirect(`/login?returnTo=${encodeURIComponent(Astro.url.pathname)}`);let test;try{test=await laboratoryReadDependencies().get.execute({actor,id:Astro.params.labTestId??''});}catch{return Astro.redirect('/404');}
---
<AppLayout title={`Review ${test.labTestNo}`}><h1>Laboratory review</h1><p>{test.labTestNo} · Submitted context version {test.version.toString()}</p><section><h2>Read-only submission context</h2><p>Measurements: {test.measurements.length}; samples: {test.samples.length}</p><p>Reviewers cannot edit submitted measurements. Review and approval require server-side permissions, SoD, current version, and approved policy.</p><p>Reject (TR-LAB-007) is a controlled workflow decision with a required reason and separation of duties. It is not a scientific FAIL result: the official result is evaluated only by the approved source. Reject decision authority itself requires an approved policy source (POLICY / SCIENTIFIC SOURCE REQUIRED) and is denied by default.</p></section></AppLayout><style>section{padding:1rem;background:var(--surface-panel);border:1px solid var(--color-border-subtle)}</style>
